Notes on the possibility of a moral law

    break point, tasks to the moral break point:
        + raise the moral-breaking problem
            • no moral law (from the design explanantia) is inferable
                ∵ no principle (by a design explanans) is determined
                    ∵ the motive reason in both design explanantia is indeterminate
                    ∵ no command/principle to employ the safehold is inferable
                        ∵ it may have been given merely as a means, subject to prudence
                            / see for instance how it figures as a means in the coincidence of (6)
                ∵ (case of mundane design) no principle qua absolute is inferable
                    ∵ possibly ∃ a (cosmos or other) context wherein the principle is not obligatory
                        ∵ the scope of obligation/command is not universal
                            : see `^*admit.+a qualification of scope.+re the case of mundane creators` @
                              02.wrong_rhetoric/._/text.notes.brec
                            ∵ the scope of creation/design is not universal
    conclusion, tasks toward the moral conclusion:
        + enter rebasing (wholly or partly) on a truth of reason/logic
            - as a recourse in response to the moral-breaking problem
                : re `moral-breaking problem` see `^*\+ raise the ${same}$`
            - either to backstop the command-based explication|interpretation of moral law against
              its shortcomings, or replace it entirely with logic-based explication|interpretation
            : cf. `^*employ\+ this \*truth of.+reason/logic\* grounding of moral law` @
              02.wrong_rhetoric/._/text.notes.brec
